</math> from each side of the given equation yields <math alttext="3 x minus 12 equals 30 minus 12"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn></math>, or <math alttext="3 x minus 12 equals 18"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn></math>. Therefore, the value of <math alttext="3 x minus 12"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn></math> is <math alttext="18"><mn>18</mn>
