    ($SATQ$441558e7$SATQ$, $SATQ$0f9a48e3-fac3-492a-8104-05def2d974ce$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$ce1ebe98-998f-4b49-ab06-cb2f5222c39f$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Algebra$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, $SATQ$H.B.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Linear functions$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Scientists collected fallen acorns that each housed a colony of the ant species <em>P. ohioensis</em>&nbsp;and analyzed each colony's structure. For any of these colonies, if the colony has <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
